The icon wrapper is inflated only where it is used

0017 turned LEGACY_ICON_TREATMENT off and the first clean install after it
could not reach the home screen: every start, the loader thread died with

  Resources$NotFoundException: drawable/adaptive_icon_drawable_wrapper
  Caused by: ClassNotFoundException: com.android.launcher3.graphics.FixedScaleDrawable
    at LauncherIcons.createBadgedIconBitmap(LauncherIcons.java:110)
    at IconCache.makeDefaultIcon -> LoaderTask.loadAllApps

createBadgedIconBitmap() inflates res/drawable-v26/adaptive_icon_drawable_wrapper.xml
for every icon the cache misses, whatever the flag says. The wrapper's
foreground is <com.android.launcher3.graphics.FixedScaleDrawable/>, and with
the treatment off wrapToAdaptiveIconDrawable() returns before touching it, so
that method stopped being a reference to the class and the shrinker dropped
it. The resource went on naming a class that was no longer in the APK, and the
very first icon -- the default one -- threw.

So the flag changed what the build keeps, not only what the code does. Nothing
would have caught it before a device: the build succeeds, every test passes,
and the APK is missing one class that only an XML file names.

The fix is not a keep rule. The wrapper is inflated to ask it for the adaptive
icon mask, the mask is passed to IconNormalizer only to fill outShape, and
outShape is read only by the wrapping branch. With the treatment off the whole
block is dead work -- an AdaptiveIconDrawable inflated and a mask built per
cache miss, on one core, for a boolean nobody reads. Both call sites now enter
it only when the treatment is on, and take the same path as a pre-O icon
otherwise, which is what they already did for applications that target below
O. FixedScaleDrawable is then legitimately unreferenced and may go.

